-- title:
--   Supersingular-polar differential with prescribed mod p q-expansion
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing every unit $u$ with $\mathrm{unitsMap}$ image $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ (for the divisibility $M/p \mid M$). Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra structure. Let $f$ be a weight-$2$ cusp form for [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained by pushing forward along $\Gamma_0(M) \hookrightarrow \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the preimage of $H$ under the lower-right-entry character $\Gamma_0(M) \to (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. Assume $f$ lies in [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p ⊥`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54): for every $t$ in the subring of endomorphisms generated by the Hecke generators, every Atkin–Lehner datum at $p$ for $M$ (an $R$ with $M = pR$ together with $a,b \in \mathbb{Z}$ satisfying $pa - Rb = 1$) and every $n$, the $n$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $t f$ and of the weight-$2$ Atkin–Lehner slash of $t f$ lies in the bottom subring of $\mathbb{C}$. Let $pf \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ satisfy $\mathrm{IsIntegralQExp}$ for $f$, i.e. its image in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ is the $q$-expansion of $f$ of width $1$. Write $\Gamma' =$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH (M/p) (ModularCurve.infSubgroup p M H hpM)`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the analogous group for the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and let $F =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ'`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) be the intermediate field of $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g$ of coefficientwise reductions of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight on $\Gamma'$ (with nonzero denominator). Then there exists $\omega \in \Omega^1_{F/K}$ which is regular at every place of $F/K$ outside [`ModularCurve.ssPlacesQExp K Γ' p`](def/ModularCurve_XHDifferentialsModL.html#L27) and has at most a simple pole at each place in that set, such that $\mathrm{diffQExp}$ applied to $\omega$ — the lift to $\Omega^1_{F/K}$ of the derivation $q\,d/dq$ on $K((q))$ restricted to $F$ — equals the Laurent series $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,pf$, the coefficientwise reduction of $pf$ in $K((q))$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the mod $p$ reduction of two-cusp integral weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_H(M)$, $p \Vert M$, onto differentials on the component through $\infty$ of the special fibre, with poles confined to the supersingular places and simple there. It is used by [`CuspForm.exists_infReductionMap_and_wReductionMap_range_le_ssPolarDifferentials`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_infReductionMap_and_wReductionMap_range_le_ssPolarDifferentials) and [`CuspForm.exists_isInfReductionMap_range_eq_ssPolarDifferentials`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_isInfReductionMap_range_eq_ssPolarDifferentials), where the corresponding reduction maps are constructed; uniqueness of $\omega$ comes from injectivity of $\mathrm{diffQExp}$.
